    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33114" root="فحج" body-key="f">
    
      5 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَفَحُّجٌ</span></b>  signifies The <i>parting of one's legs,</i>
or <i>making an opening between them,</i> (AA, S, O,
K,) <i>when sitting;</i> as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَفْحِيجٌ</span></b> : like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَفَشُّجٌ</span>
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَفْشِيجٌ</span>. (AA, S, O.) And one says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَتَفَحَّجُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَاقَاهُ</span> [<i>His shanks are parted</i>]. (S, O.) See also 1.

